Z||000000||jazer||03-10-2001||12:15 AM||||Will a turbo from 3.8 V6 Grand National work with my 2.8??||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||03-10-2001||10:58 PM||||It might be too big, but you could try it. What kind is it?<BR>You <I>do</I> know how much work/money is involved in a turbo install, don't you?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||03-11-2001||05:28 PM||||If you got deep pockets anything will work.  If you do it start out at low boost, don't over do it.  Slowley work your way up. Turning up boost to quickly can do a lot of damage in a hurry! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||03-12-2001||11:12 AM||||The GN turbo is WAY too big.  It put out 19 pounds of boost on the 3.8L! (with Hypertech chip).  It's a huge turbo, but I forget the model.  If you used it with a lower boost pressure, you're just wasting your time, because it takes a bit to get spooled up since it's so big.  ||||reg||1
